@* shadcn's responsive example renders a Dialog on a desktop and a Drawer on a phone, chosen in
   React from a media query. Static SSR has no such hook — and needs none: both are the same
   <dialog>, so one element with a media query on its frame is the whole thing. Below 640px it
   comes up from the bottom and can be dragged away; above, it is a centred modal. *@
<DrawerTrigger Target="drawer-responsive">Open</DrawerTrigger>

<Drawer Id="drawer-responsive"
        Class="sm:!inset-auto sm:!top-1/2 sm:!left-1/2 sm:!max-w-lg sm:!-translate-x-1/2 sm:!-translate-y-1/2 sm:!rounded-lg">
    <DrawerHeader>
        <DrawerTitle>Move to project</DrawerTitle>
        <DrawerDescription>A sheet on a phone, a dialog on a desktop, one element.</DrawerDescription>
    </DrawerHeader>
    <DrawerFooter>
        <Button>Move</Button>
        <DrawerClose>Cancel</DrawerClose>
    </DrawerFooter>
</Drawer>
